// The rules of Mary-O's rooms (schema `room_rules`). Her plugin declares
// them for the rooms of its scope. An edit here is played at the next start,
// with no Rust build.
(
    // How long the level holds on her death before it starts again. Sized by
    // the music, not by taste: `mary_o_you_died` is four bars of 2/4 at 150
    // bpm (eight beats, 3.2 s), and its last chord is the low thud the whole
    // cue exists to land. If the score's tempo or bar count changes, this
    // number changes with it.
    replay_level_after_death_s: Some(3.2),
    // How near she must be for an enemy to keep thinking. It clears the
    // half-width of the widest view a player can select, so no enemy comes
    // into frame already moving: the presets are 640/800/960/1120/1600 wide,
    // `Cinematic`'s 560 half-width is the widest PLAY choice, and 720 clears
    // it by 160 (five tiles). `Debug`'s 800 is not cleared on purpose: content
    // sized for that zoom would let the rule sleep nothing.
    // (`the_wake_radius_clears_the_widest_playable_view` reads the presets.)
    // Her enemies patrol, and none is worth a brain on the far side of the
    // level. A kicked shell still slides when it is far: dormancy sleeps the
    // brain, and the shell's slide writes the body's velocity on another
    // channel.
    hostile_wake_radius: Some(720.0),
)
